<h2>Entities</h2>

<p>
The SmartCGMS architecture recognizes the following types of entities:
<ul>
    <li>{doclink('api','filter','filters')|noescape} - a base entity, maintains one isolated piece of work</li>
    <li>{doclink('api','discretemodel','discrete models')|noescape} - generates signals with a fixed stepping</li>
    <li>{doclink('api','signalmodel','signal models')|noescape} - generates signals as a result of another incoming signal level</li>
    <li>{doclink('api','metric','metrics')|noescape} - evaluates the differences between two signals</li>
    <li>{doclink('api','solver','solvers')|noescape} - optimizes parameters of a given model using a programmer-defined objective function</li>
    <li>{doclink('api','approximator','approximators')|noescape} - approximates a discrete signal, calculates (or estimates) its derivation</li>
    <li>{doclink('api','signal','signals')|noescape} - containers for a set of signal levels</li>
</ul>
</p>

<p>
Each entity has its own GUID and descriptor. A single entity should be managed by a single shared object (dynamic library). The shared object that exported the entity descriptor
(via the <code>do_get_*_descriptors</code>) must also be able to create it using appropriate factory method (<code>do_create_*</code>).
</p>

<p>
Some entity types must implement its respective interface. If using the C++ SDK, the interface identifiers per entity type are as follows:
<ul>
    <li><code>scgms::IFilter</code> for {doclink('api','filter','filters')|noescape}</li>
    <li><code>scgms::IDiscrete_Model</code> for {doclink('api','discretemodel','discrete models')|noescape}</li>
    <li><code>scgms::IMetric</code> for {doclink('api','metric','metrics')|noescape}</li>
    <li><code>scgms::IApproximator</code> for <a href="?page=apiapproximator">approximators</a></li>
    <li><code>scgms::ISignal</code> for {doclink('api','signal','signals')|noescape}</li>

    <li>{doclink('api','signalmodel','signal models')|noescape} are not exported as entities; instead, they only manage a collection of {doclink('api','signal','signals')|noescape} (thus a signal model has a descriptor and available signals only)</li>
    <li>{doclink('api','solver','solvers')|noescape} are not exported as entities; instead, they are invoked using <code>do_solve_generic</code> call</li>
</ul>
</p>

<p>
Interface contracts, descriptor contents and implementation details are described in respective subpages.
</p>
